The adapted definitions are the finite-lattice site, Laplacian, mass-operator
and spectral-covariance definitions in
AImathPPhi2Clean/ConcreteLatticeOperator.lean.  Their correspondence with the
pinned upstream commit is checked, file by file and body by body, by
audit/check_upstream_finite_definitions.py (with two deliberate-corruption
negative controls that the check must reject).  That check is a textual
provenance test; it is not a proof, and the Lean theorems in this repository
stand on their own proofs.

The remaining modules are original to this project, except where a file header
says otherwise (the Wick, layer-cake, tightness and reconstruction modules name
their upstream sources in their headers).

